  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here are the key files that make up the Bookmarks page UI in Grafana:\n\n---\n\n### Primary Page Component\n\n- **`public/app/features/bookmarks/BookmarksPage.tsx`** — This is the main (and only) file in the bookmarks feature folder. It renders the full bookmarks page, including:\n  - An empty state with a call-to-action when there are no bookmarks\n  - A responsive CSS grid of `NavLandingPageCard` components for each bookmarked item\n  - It resolves bookmarked URLs into nav model items via `findByUrl` against the nav tree\n\n---\n\n### Data / State Layer\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/hooks.ts`** — Contains the `usePinnedItems` hook that the bookmarks page uses to fetch the list of bookmarked URLs. It reads from user preferences via the RTK Query hook `useGetUserPreferencesQuery`, specifically `preferences.data?.navbar?.bookmarkUrls`.\n\n---\n\n### Supporting Utility\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/utils.ts`** — Contains the `findByUrl` function (lines 161-173) used by the bookmarks page to look up a `NavModelItem` from the nav tree by URL. Also contains `getActiveItem` which has bookmark-specific logic (lines 126-128) to avoid searching parent items in the bookmarks section.\n\n---\n\n### Card Component (each bookmark tile)\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/NavLandingPage/NavLandingPageCard.tsx`** — The card component used to render each individual bookmark. Displays a heading (text) and description, with optional category-based color styling. Each card links to the bookmarked URL via `href`.\n\n---\n\n### Routing\n\n- **`public/app/routes/routes.tsx`** (lines 537-541) — Registers the `/bookmarks` route, lazy-loading the `BookmarksPage` component:\n\n```537:541:public/app/routes/routes.tsx\n    {\n      path: '/bookmarks',\n      component: SafeDynamicImport(\n        () => import(/* webpackChunkName: \"BookmarksPage\"*/ 'app/features/bookmarks/BookmarksPage')\n      ),\n    },\n```\n\n---\n\n### Mega Menu Integration (pinning/unpinning bookmarks)\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenuItemText.tsx`** — Renders the bookmark pin/unpin icon next to nav menu items in the sidebar mega menu (the mechanism users use to add/remove bookmarks).\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenu.tsx`** — The mega menu itself, which renders the bookmarks section within the navigation sidebar.\n\n---\n\n### Nav Bar Tree (Redux state)\n\n- **`public/app/core/reducers/navBarTree.ts`** — The Redux reducer managing the navigation tree state, which includes the `bookmarks` nav node. The bookmarks page reads from this state via `useSelector`.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n| Concern | File |\n|---|---|\n| Page component & layout | `public/app/features/bookmarks/BookmarksPage.tsx` |\n| Bookmark data hook | `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/hooks.ts` |\n| URL-to-nav lookup | `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/utils.ts` |\n| Bookmark card tile | `public/app/core/components/NavLandingPage/NavLandingPageCard.tsx` |\n| Route definition | `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` |\n| Pin/unpin UI in sidebar | `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenuItemText.tsx` |\n| Sidebar bookmark section | `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenu.tsx` |\n| Nav tree Redux state | `public/app/core/reducers/navBarTree.ts` |\n\nThe simplest starting point for UI changes to the bookmarks page itself is `BookmarksPage.tsx`. If you want to change how bookmark cards look, modify `NavLandingPageCard.tsx`. For changes to how bookmarks are stored or fetched, look at `hooks.ts` and the user preferences API.",
