  "text": "\nThe browse-dashboards migration is done. Summary:\n\n## Summary\n\n### 1. Feature flag\n- Added `browseDashboardsUseNavigate` in `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go`\n- Ran `make gen-feature-toggles` to update generated files\n\n### 2. CreateNewButton.tsx\n- Imported `useNavigate` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`\n- Added `const navigate = useNavigate()` in the component\n- Replaced `locationService.push` with a feature-flag check that uses `navigate()` when enabled\n\n### 3. FolderActionsButton.tsx\n- Imported `useNavigate` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` and `config` from `@grafana/runtime`\n- Added `const navigate = useNavigate()` in the component\n- Replaced `locationService.push` with a feature-flag check that uses `navigate()` when enabled\n\n### 4. Tests\n- Added `useNavigate` mocks in both test files\n- Reset `config.featureToggles.browseDashboardsUseNavigate = false` in `beforeEach` and `afterEach`\n\n### 5. Verification\n- All 17 browse-dashboards test suites pass (145 tests)\n- No linter errors\n\n### Not migrated\n- **browseDashboardsAPI.ts**: `locationService.push` remains in the RTK Query `onQueryStarted` callback because it is not inside a React component and cannot use hooks.\n\nTo enable the new behavior, set `browseDashboardsUseNavigate` to `true` in the feature flags.",
